  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<font size='3'>City of Brampton 2016 Spring Orthophoto was captured on March 19, 2016 at 10 cm resolution <span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.42px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);'>and orthorectified. An orthophoto, orthophotograph or orthoimage is an aerial photograph geometrically corrected (&quot;orthorectified&quot;) such that the scale is uniform: the photo has the same lack of distortion as a map. Unlike an uncorrected aerial photograph, an orthophotograph can be used to measure true distances, because it is an accurate representation of the Earth's surface, having been adjusted for topographic relief, lens distortion, and camera tilt. - </span></font><a href='# the photo has the same lack of distortion as a map. Unlike an uncorrected aerial photograph, an orthophotograph can be used to measure true distances, because it is an accurate representation of the Earth' target='_blank'>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orthophoto</a>"
